From: chengyingw <1424556745@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:28:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Gate KB claim writes on executable checks

Claims may carry checks replayed on stored measurements whenever they are
written. Merge and revise inherit every ancestor check and are written only if
all pass; a failing check rejects an add; too little data or a mixed result is
never a falsification. Delete in propose_changes now needs evidence, and a
counterexample must be a solve that cited this claim version and lost credit.

Checks read --lab, comparing only inside one set_id, or --check-table result
tables with count, position and ratio. Claims without checks behave as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
